response:
I assumed r03's layout carries over: tickets in spe/evals/tasks/tickets/, configs in triage/configs/B/ and triage/configs/C2/, and a tool shim at triage/bin/tool. Each of these paths is an arg you can override.

**Gates before launch.** I run 4 gates in order. First, I confirm that spe/predictions/r04.yaml and spe/plans/r04.md are in HEAD and unchanged since the commit 10 minutes ago. Second, I run the grader selftest on spe/evals/graders/grade.py. An oracle file built from spe/evals/tasks/answers.json must score 50 of 50. An empty file must score 0, and so must a file with every label shifted. The same check confirms that answers.json holds 50 tickets, as the plan says. If it holds 40, I halt and ask you. Third, I regrade r03's saved outputs with this grader as a control. The scores must match r03's recorded scores, because any shift is a grader change and not an agent change. Fourth, I dry run the script with `args.only` set to 3 cell keys (1 B and 2 C2), `trials: 1` and `capUSD: 2`. Each trial must return schema-valid output. The leak scan must find all 3 transcripts with no peeks. grade.py and the judge must each return one row per trial. I also check the measured cost per trial. If 500 trials at that cost plus the $6 reserve would go over $40, I halt and ask you. When all 4 gates pass, I commit spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js locally with a plain message and no co-author line. I push nothing. Then I launch with `{round: 'r04'}`.

```js
// spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js
export const meta = {
  name: 'triage-spe-eval',
  description: 'SPE eval for the triage support agent. Runs each config on each ticket, scans transcripts for answer-key reads, grades category and priority with grade.py, judges reply tone with Opus, tops up split cells, and ends with failure analysis and a completeness critic. The round comes from args.round.',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Load' },
    { title: 'Trials' },
    { title: 'Leak scan' },
    { title: 'Grade' },
    { title: 'Judge' },
    { title: 'Top-up' },
    { title: 'Synthesis' },
  ],
};

// ---------- arguments ----------
const A = typeof args === 'object' && args ? args : {};
const ROUND = A.round ?? 'r04';
const CONFIGS = A.configs ?? {
  B:  { model: 'sonnet', prompt: 'triage/configs/B/prompt.md',  tools: 'triage/configs/B/tools.json' },
  C2: { model: 'sonnet', prompt: 'triage/configs/C2/prompt.md', tools: 'triage/configs/C2/tools.json' },
};
const TICKET_DIR     = A.ticketDir ?? 'spe/evals/tasks/tickets';
const EXPECT_TICKETS = A.expectTickets ?? 50;
const TRIALS         = A.trials ?? 5;
const TOPUP_PER_CELL = A.topUpPerCell ?? 5;   // extra trials for each split cell
const TOPUP_CELLS    = A.topUpCells ?? 20;    // most split cells that get a top-up
const CAP            = A.capUSD ?? 40;
const RESERVE        = A.reserveUSD ?? 6;     // held back for scan, grade, judge, synthesis
// Unmeasured per-call estimates. The dry run measures real values, which go in args.est.
const EST = { load: 0.30, trial: 0.05, scan: 0.25, grade: 0.15, judge: 0.20, synth: 0.80, ...(A.est ?? {}) };
const GRADE_CMD    = A.gradeCmd ?? 'python spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json';
const JUDGE_RUBRIC = A.judgeRubric ?? 'spe/evals/graders/judge.md';
const TOOL_SHIM    = A.toolShim ?? 'triage/bin/tool';
const TRANSCRIPTS  = A.transcriptDir ?? '~/.claude/projects';
const SCRATCH      = A.scratch ?? `/tmp/triage-spe-${ROUND}`;
const JUDGE_BATCH  = A.judgeBatch ?? 25;
const ONLY         = Array.isArray(A.only) ? new Set(A.only) : null;
const SUPPORT_MODEL = 'opus';   // non-trial agents use Opus
const JUDGE_MODEL   = 'opus';   // named in the approved plan

// ---------- helpers ----------
const range  = (n) => Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => i);
const chunk  = (xs, size) => range(Math.ceil(xs.length / size)).map((i) => xs.slice(i * size, (i + 1) * size));
const groupBy = (xs, f) => xs.reduce((m, x) => { (m[f(x)] ??= []).push(x); return m; }, {});
const mean   = (xs) => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / xs.length : null);
const median = (xs) => {
  if (!xs.length) return null;
  const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b); const m = s.length >> 1;
  return s.length % 2 ? s[m] : (s[m - 1] + s[m]) / 2;
};
const r3 = (x) => (x == null ? null : Math.round(x * 1000) / 1000);
const KEY_PATTERN = /(^|[\s'"\/])spe\/|answers\.json|grade\.py|judge\.md/;

let spent = 0;
let halt = null;
const skipped = [];
const voided = [];
const notes = [];

function setHalt(reason, detail) {
  if (!halt || (halt.reason === 'budget' && reason !== 'budget')) halt = { reason, detail };
  log(`HALT (${reason}): ${detail}`);
}

// Reserve the estimate before the call. Trials may use only CAP minus RESERVE.
function canSpend(cost, id, pool) {
  const limit = pool === 'trials' ? CAP - RESERVE : CAP;
  if (spent + cost > limit) {
    skipped.push({ id, estUSD: cost, spentUSD: r3(spent), limitUSD: limit });
    log(`SKIP ${id}: estimated spend $${(spent + cost).toFixed(2)} would cross $${limit}`);
    if (!halt) setHalt('budget', `cap $${CAP} (trial pool $${CAP - RESERVE}) reached at about $${spent.toFixed(2)}`);
    return false;
  }
  spent += cost;
  return true;
}

async function tryAgent(prompt, opts, retries = 1) {
  for (let i = 0; ; i++) {
    try { return await agent(prompt, opts); }
    catch (e) {
      if (i >= retries) throw e;
      log(`retry ${opts.label}: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 120)}`);
    }
  }
}

// ---------- schemas ----------
const str = { type: 'string' };
const LOAD_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['tickets', 'configs'],
  properties: {
    tickets: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['id', 'text'], properties: { id: str, text: str } } },
    configs: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['name', 'prompt', 'tools'], properties: { name: str, prompt: str, tools: str } } },
  },
};
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['label', 'reply', 'tool_calls', 'tool_errors', 'paths_read'],
  properties: {
    label: {
      type: 'object', required: ['category', 'priority'],
      properties: {
        category: { enum: ['billing', 'bug', 'how-to', 'account', 'outage'] },
        priority: { enum: ['P1', 'P2', 'P3', 'P4'] },
      },
    },
    reply: str,
    tool_calls: { type: 'integer', minimum: 0 },
    tool_errors: { type: 'integer', minimum: 0 },
    tools_used: { type: 'array', items: str },
    paths_read: { type: 'array', items: str },
  },
};
const SCAN_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['results'],
  properties: { results: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial', 'found', 'peeks'],
    properties: { trial: str, found: { type: 'boolean' }, peeks: { type: 'array', items: str }, tokens: { type: ['integer', 'null'] } } } } },
};
const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['results'],
  properties: {
    error: str,
    results: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial', 'category_ok', 'priority_ok'],
      properties: { trial: str, category_ok: { type: 'boolean' }, priority_ok: { type: 'boolean' } } } },
  },
};
const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['results'],
  properties: { results: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['trial', 'tone_score', 'tone_pass', 'reason'],
    properties: { trial: str, tone_score: { type: 'number' }, tone_pass: { type: 'boolean' }, reason: str } } } },
};
const ANALYSIS_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['failures', 'proposals'],
  properties: {
    failures: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['id', 'mode', 'configs', 'examples', 'cause'],
      properties: { id: str, mode: str, configs: { type: 'object', additionalProperties: { type: 'integer' } }, examples: { type: 'array', items: str }, cause: str } } },
    proposals: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', required: ['change', 'targets', 'why'],
      properties: { change: str, targets: { type: 'array', items: str }, why: str } } },
  },
};
const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: 'object', required: ['complete', 'gaps'],
  properties: { complete: { type: 'boolean' }, gaps: { type: 'array', items: str }, rerun: { type: 'array', items: str } },
};

// ---------- Load ----------
phase('Load');
spent += EST.load;
const loaded = await tryAgent([
  'You load inputs for an eval harness. Copy text verbatim. Do not summarize or edit anything.',
  `1. Read every ticket file in ${TICKET_DIR}. Return each ticket's id (the file name without extension) and its full text.`,
  `2. Read these config files and return each config's name, prompt text, and tools text: ${JSON.stringify(CONFIGS)}`,
  'Do not open spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, anything in spe/evals/graders/, or anything in spe/predictions/.',
].join('\n'), { label: 'load', phase: 'Load', schema: LOAD_SCHEMA, model: SUPPORT_MODEL });

const tickets = [...loaded.tickets].sort((a, b) => a.id.localeCompare(b.id));
const TICKET_TEXT = Object.fromEntries(tickets.map((t) => [t.id, t.text]));
const CFG_TEXT = Object.fromEntries(loaded.configs.map((c) => [c.name, c]));
if (!ONLY && tickets.length !== EXPECT_TICKETS) {
  throw new Error(`Halt: found ${tickets.length} tickets in ${TICKET_DIR}, the approved plan says ${EXPECT_TICKETS}. Ask the user which set to run.`);
}
for (const name of Object.keys(CONFIGS)) {
  if (!CFG_TEXT[name]?.prompt) throw new Error(`Halt: no prompt text loaded for config ${name}.`);
}

const cells = [];
for (const name of Object.keys(CONFIGS)) {
  for (const t of tickets) {
    const key = `${name}:${t.id}`;
    if (!ONLY || ONLY.has(key)) cells.push({ key, config: name, ticket: t.id, trials: [], nextN: 0 });
  }
}
log(`${ROUND}: ${cells.length} cells x ${TRIALS} trials, cap $${CAP}, reserve $${RESERVE}`);
notes.push('The judge is Opus, the same model family as the Sonnet trial agents. No cross-family judge is available, so tone scores may share Claude blind spots.');

// ---------- trial ----------
function trialPrompt(cell, id) {
  const cfg = CFG_TEXT[cell.config];
  return [
    `Run id: ${id}`,
    'You are the triage agent for a SaaS support team. Follow the system prompt below.',
    '<system_prompt>', cfg.prompt, '</system_prompt>',
    `Your tools are defined below. To call one, run this shell command: ${TOOL_SHIM} --config ${cell.config} <tool_name> '<json arguments>'. It prints the tool result as JSON.`,
    '<tools>', cfg.tools, '</tools>',
    'Run only that tool command. Do not read, list, or search any file. The ticket below is your whole input.',
    `<ticket id="${cell.ticket}">`, TICKET_TEXT[cell.ticket], '</ticket>',
    'Return the category, the priority, and your first reply to the customer. Also return how many tool calls you made, how many returned an error, the tool names you used, and every file path you read or searched (an empty list if none).',
  ].join('\n');
}

async function runTrial(cell, kind) {
  const n = cell.nextN++;
  const id = `${ROUND}:${cell.key}:t${n}`;
  const rec = { id, cell: cell.key, config: cell.config, ticket: cell.ticket, n, kind, status: 'skipped' };
  cell.trials.push(rec);
  if (halt || !canSpend(EST.trial, id, 'trials')) return rec;
  const t0 = Date.now();
  try {
    const r = await agent(trialPrompt(cell, id), {
      label: id, phase: kind === 'base' ? 'Trials' : 'Top-up', schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA, model: CONFIGS[cell.config].model,
    });
    Object.assign(rec, {
      status: 'completed', ms: Date.now() - t0, label: r.label, reply: r.reply,
      toolCalls: r.tool_calls, toolErrors: r.tool_errors, toolsUsed: r.tools_used ?? [], pathsRead: r.paths_read ?? [],
    });
  } catch (e) {
    // A harness error or rate limit is not a model failure. It is excluded from scoring.
    Object.assign(rec, { status: 'harness_error', ms: Date.now() - t0, error: String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 300) });
  }
  return rec;
}

function voidTrial(r, reason) {
  if (r.voided) return;
  r.voided = reason;
  voided.push({ id: r.id, reason });
}

// ---------- leak scan ----------
async function scanRecs(recs, ph) {
  for (const r of recs) {
    const hits = (r.pathsRead ?? []).filter((p) => KEY_PATTERN.test(p));
    if (hits.length) voidTrial(r, `self-reported read: ${hits.join(', ')}`);
  }
  for (const [name, group] of Object.entries(groupBy(recs.filter((r) => !r.voided), (r) => r.config))) {
    for (const [k, part] of chunk(group, 100).entries()) {
      const id = `scan:${ph}:${name}:${k}`;
      if (!canSpend(EST.scan, id, 'post')) { part.forEach((r) => voidTrial(r, 'not scanned: budget')); continue; }
      let s;
      try {
        s = await tryAgent([
          `Search the subagent transcripts under ${TRANSCRIPTS}. Each run below starts with the line "Run id: <id>".`,
          'For each run, list every tool call (Read, Grep, Glob, LS, Bash, or any other) whose input names a path under spe/, or names answers.json, grade.py, or judge.md.',
          'Set found to false when you cannot find the run. Report the run\'s total tokens if the transcript records usage, otherwise null.',
          'Runs:', ...part.map((r) => r.id),
        ].join('\n'), { label: id, phase: ph, schema: SCAN_SCHEMA, model: SUPPORT_MODEL });
      } catch (e) {
        part.forEach((r) => voidTrial(r, `not scanned: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 80)}`));
        continue;
      }
      const got = new Map(s.results.map((x) => [x.trial, x]));
      for (const r of part) {
        const x = got.get(r.id);
        if (!x || !x.found) voidTrial(r, 'transcript not found');
        else if (x.peeks.length) voidTrial(r, `peeked: ${x.peeks.join('; ')}`);
        else { r.scanned = true; r.tokens = x.tokens ?? null; }
      }
    }
  }
}

// ---------- code grader ----------
async function gradeRecs(recs, ph) {
  const todo = recs.filter((r) => r.scanned && !r.voided && !r.graded);
  for (const [name, group] of Object.entries(groupBy(todo, (r) => r.config))) {
    for (const [k, part] of chunk(group, 150).entries()) {
      if (halt?.reason === 'grader') return;
      const id = `grade:${ph}:${name}:${k}`;
      if (!canSpend(EST.grade, id, 'post')) continue;
      const file = `${SCRATCH}/${ph.replace(/\W+/g, '-').toLowerCase()}-${name}-${k}.jsonl`;
      const lines = part.map((r) => JSON.stringify({ trial: r.id, ticket_id: r.ticket, label: r.label })).join('\n');
      let g;
      try {
        g = await tryAgent([
          'You run a code grader. Do not judge anything yourself.',
          `1. Write the JSON lines between the markers to ${file}, one object per line, unchanged.`,
          `2. Run: ${GRADE_CMD} ${file}`,
          '3. Return one result per input line from the grader output: trial, category_ok, priority_ok. Copy the values. Do not fix, infer, or fill any value.',
          'If the command exits non-zero or its output does not cover every trial, return error with the exit code and the first 40 lines of stderr.',
          '<<<LINES', lines, 'LINES>>>',
        ].join('\n'), { label: id, phase: ph, schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: SUPPORT_MODEL });
      } catch (e) {
        setHalt('grader', `${id} failed: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 200)}`);
        return;
      }
      const got = new Map((g.results ?? []).map((x) => [x.trial, x]));
      if (g.error || part.some((r) => !got.has(r.id))) {
        setHalt('grader', g.error ?? `${id} returned ${got.size} of ${part.length} rows`);
        return;
      }
      for (const r of part) {
        const x = got.get(r.id);
        Object.assign(r, { graded: true, categoryOk: x.category_ok, priorityOk: x.priority_ok });
      }
    }
  }
}

// ---------- tone judge (only what code cannot check) ----------
async function judgeRecs(recs, ph) {
  const todo = recs.filter((r) => r.graded && !r.voided && r.tonePass == null);
  await parallel(chunk(todo, JUDGE_BATCH).map((part, k) => async () => {
    const id = `judge:${ph}:${k}`;
    if (!canSpend(EST.judge, id, 'post')) return;
    try {
      const j = await tryAgent([
        `Read ${JUDGE_RUBRIC} and apply it to each reply below. Score tone only, as the rubric defines it.`,
        'Do not score category or priority. Do not read any other file.',
        'Return one result per trial id: the rubric score, pass or fail, and one sentence of reason.',
        ...part.map((r) => `<item trial="${r.id}">\n<ticket>\n${TICKET_TEXT[r.ticket]}\n</ticket>\n<reply>\n${r.reply}\n</reply>\n</item>`),
      ].join('\n'), { label: id, phase: ph, schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL });
      const got = new Map(j.results.map((x) => [x.trial, x]));
      for (const r of part) {
        const x = got.get(r.id);
        if (x) Object.assign(r, { toneScore: x.tone_score, tonePass: x.tone_pass, toneReason: x.reason });
      }
    } catch (e) {
      notes.push(`${id} failed, ${part.length} replies unjudged: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 120)}`);
    }
  }));
}

async function postProcess(recs, phScan, phGrade, phJudge) {
  if (phScan) phase(phScan);
  await scanRecs(recs, phScan ?? phGrade);
  if (phGrade !== phScan) phase(phGrade);
  await gradeRecs(recs, phGrade);
  if (halt?.reason === 'grader') return;
  if (phJudge !== phGrade) phase(phJudge);
  await judgeRecs(recs, phJudge);
}

// ---------- Trials ----------
phase('Trials');
const baseRecs = await parallel(cells.flatMap((c) => range(TRIALS).map(() => () => runTrial(c, 'base'))));
await postProcess(baseRecs.filter((r) => r.status === 'completed'), 'Leak scan', 'Grade', 'Judge');

// ---------- Top-up ----------
const valid = (r) => r.status === 'completed' && !r.voided && r.graded;
const labelPass = (r) => r.categoryOk && r.priorityOk;
const baseValid = (c) => c.trials.filter((r) => r.kind !== 'topup' && valid(r));

phase('Top-up');
if (!halt) {
  const jobs = [];
  const split = [];
  for (const c of cells) {
    const v = baseValid(c);
    const lost = TRIALS - v.length;   // harness errors and voided trials get one refill
    for (let i = 0; i < lost; i++) jobs.push(() => runTrial(c, 'refill'));
    const p = v.filter(labelPass).length;
    if (p > 0 && p < v.length) split.push(c);
  }
  const chosen = split.slice(0, TOPUP_CELLS);
  if (split.length > chosen.length) {
    notes.push(`${split.length} split cells, top-up cap ${TOPUP_CELLS}. Not topped up: ${split.slice(TOPUP_CELLS).map((c) => c.key).join(', ')}`);
  }
  for (const c of chosen) for (let i = 0; i < TOPUP_PER_CELL; i++) jobs.push(() => runTrial(c, 'topup'));
  log(`Top-up: ${jobs.length} trials (${chosen.length} split cells, rest are refills)`);
  const fresh = (await parallel(jobs)).filter((r) => r.status === 'completed');
  await postProcess(fresh, 'Top-up', 'Top-up', 'Top-up');
} else {
  notes.push(`Top-up skipped because of halt: ${halt.reason}`);
}

// ---------- metrics ----------
// Headline accuracy uses the first TRIALS valid base or refill trials per cell, so top-up does not bias it.
function summarize(name) {
  const cs = cells.filter((c) => c.config === name);
  const all = cs.flatMap((c) => c.trials);
  const base = cs.flatMap((c) => baseValid(c).sort((a, b) => a.n - b.n).slice(0, TRIALS));
  const judged = base.filter((r) => r.tonePass != null);
  const full = cs.filter((c) => baseValid(c).length >= TRIALS);
  const topup = all.filter((r) => r.kind === 'topup' && valid(r));
  const calls = base.reduce((a, r) => a + (r.toolCalls ?? 0), 0);
  const errs = base.reduce((a, r) => a + (r.toolErrors ?? 0), 0);
  const toks = base.map((r) => r.tokens).filter((x) => typeof x === 'number');
  return {
    config: name,
    model: CONFIGS[name].model,
    counts: {
      completed: all.filter((r) => r.status === 'completed').length,
      harness_error: all.filter((r) => r.status === 'harness_error').length,
      skipped: all.filter((r) => r.status === 'skipped').length,
      voided: all.filter((r) => r.voided).length,
      scored_base: base.length,
      judged_base: judged.length,
    },
    category_acc: r3(mean(base.map((r) => (r.categoryOk ? 1 : 0)))),
    priority_acc: r3(mean(base.map((r) => (r.priorityOk ? 1 : 0)))),
    label_acc: r3(mean(base.map((r) => (labelPass(r) ? 1 : 0)))),
    tone_pass: r3(mean(judged.map((r) => (r.tonePass ? 1 : 0)))),
    tone_score_mean: r3(mean(judged.map((r) => r.toneScore))),
    cells_all_pass: r3(mean(full.map((c) => (baseValid(c).slice(0, TRIALS).every(labelPass) ? 1 : 0)))),
    median_ms: median(base.map((r) => r.ms)),
    mean_tool_calls: r3(mean(base.map((r) => r.toolCalls ?? 0))),
    tool_error_rate: calls ? r3(errs / calls) : null,
    mean_tokens: toks.length ? Math.round(mean(toks)) : null,
    tokens_coverage: base.length ? r3(toks.length / base.length) : null,
    topup: { cells: new Set(topup.map((r) => r.cell)).size, trials: topup.length, label_acc: r3(mean(topup.map((r) => (labelPass(r) ? 1 : 0)))) },
  };
}
const summary = Object.keys(CONFIGS).map(summarize);
const allRecs = cells.flatMap((c) => c.trials);
const harnessErrors = allRecs.filter((r) => r.status === 'harness_error').map((r) => ({ id: r.id, error: r.error }));

// ---------- Synthesis ----------
phase('Synthesis');
let failureAnalysis = null;
let critic = null;
if (halt?.reason === 'grader') {
  notes.push('Synthesis skipped. The grader broke, so no scores from this run are valid.');
} else {
  const failing = allRecs.filter((r) => valid(r) && (!labelPass(r) || r.tonePass === false)).map((r) => ({
    id: r.id, cell: r.cell, kind: r.kind, label: r.label, categoryOk: r.categoryOk, priorityOk: r.priorityOk,
    tonePass: r.tonePass, toneReason: r.toneReason, toolsUsed: r.toolsUsed, reply: (r.reply ?? '').slice(0, 400),
  }));
  if (canSpend(EST.synth, 'failure-analysis', 'post')) {
    try {
      failureAnalysis = await tryAgent([
        `You analyze failures from ${ROUND} of the triage agent eval. Configs: ${JSON.stringify(CONFIGS)}.`,
        'Read spe/evals/tasks/answers.json for the expected labels and spe/failures.md for the entry format. Do not read spe/predictions/.',
        `Group the failing trials into failure modes. Give each an ID of the form "${ROUND} F1", "${ROUND} F2", and so on.`,
        'For each mode, give a one-line description, the count per config, up to 3 example trial ids, and the likely cause.',
        'Separate harness errors from model failures. Harness errors are not model failures.',
        'Then propose changes for the next round. Each proposal changes one thing and names the failure IDs it targets.',
        `Summary: ${JSON.stringify(summary)}`,
        `Failing trials: ${JSON.stringify(failing)}`,
        `Harness errors: ${JSON.stringify(harnessErrors)}`,
        `Voided trials: ${JSON.stringify(voided)}`,
      ].join('\n'), { label: 'failure-analysis', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: ANALYSIS_SCHEMA, model: SUPPORT_MODEL });
    } catch (e) {
      notes.push(`failure-analysis failed: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 120)}`);
    }
  }
  if (canSpend(EST.synth, 'completeness-critic', 'post')) {
    try {
      critic = await tryAgent([
        `You check whether the ${ROUND} eval results are complete enough to score against the predictions. Do not read spe/predictions/.`,
        `Plan: configs ${Object.keys(CONFIGS).join(' and ')}, ${EXPECT_TICKETS} tickets, ${TRIALS} trials per cell, cap $${CAP}.`,
        'Check each item and list every gap:',
        `- Every cell has ${TRIALS} scored base trials, or a logged reason why not.`,
        '- Every scored trial has a code grade and a tone judgment.',
        '- Harness errors and voided trials are excluded from accuracy.',
        '- Every metric has a value, including runtime, tool calls, tool errors, and tokens.',
        '- Budget skips and halts are logged.',
        '- The failure analysis covers every failing trial and separates harness errors.',
        'List cells to rerun, if any.',
        `Summary: ${JSON.stringify(summary)}`,
        `Halt: ${JSON.stringify(halt)}`,
        `Skipped: ${JSON.stringify(skipped)}`,
        `Voided: ${JSON.stringify(voided)}`,
        `Notes: ${JSON.stringify(notes)}`,
        `Failure analysis: ${JSON.stringify(failureAnalysis)}`,
      ].join('\n'), { label: 'completeness-critic', phase: 'Synthesis', schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: SUPPORT_MODEL });
    } catch (e) {
      notes.push(`completeness-critic failed: ${String(e?.message ?? e).slice(0, 120)}`);
    }
  }
}

log(`${ROUND} done. Estimated spend $${spent.toFixed(2)} of $${CAP}. Halt: ${halt ? halt.reason : 'none'}`);

return {
  round: ROUND,
  halt,
  spend: { estimatedUSD: r3(spent), capUSD: CAP, note: 'Estimated from args.est. Check it against the console bill.' },
  summary,
  skipped,
  voided,
  harnessErrors,
  failureAnalysis,
  critic,
  notes,
  trials: allRecs.map((r) => ({
    id: r.id, cell: r.cell, config: r.config, ticket: r.ticket, n: r.n, kind: r.kind, status: r.status,
    voided: r.voided ?? null, label: r.label ?? null, categoryOk: r.categoryOk ?? null, priorityOk: r.priorityOk ?? null,
    toneScore: r.toneScore ?? null, tonePass: r.tonePass ?? null, toneReason: r.toneReason ?? null,
    ms: r.ms ?? null, toolCalls: r.toolCalls ?? null, toolErrors: r.toolErrors ?? null, tokens: r.tokens ?? null,
    reply: r.reply ?? null,
  })),
};
```

Three things in this script are guesses that I could not check from here. The dry run is the gate that tests them.
- The command-line flags for grade.py are in `args.gradeCmd`.
- The transcript location is in `args.transcriptDir`. If the leak scan cannot find the transcripts, it voids those trials, so a wrong path will show up in the dry run.
- The per-call cost estimates are in `args.est`. They have not been measured.
